## What was wrong

The compile gate (`longrun/bin/dispatch360.py::compile_gate`) runs `lake env lean <abs path>` for every `.lean` file with **the worktree root as cwd**. That root had no `lean-toolchain`/lakefile/`.lake`, so elan aborted all 68 compilations with `no default toolchain configured` (exit 1) — even though every authored file compiled fine from `release/`. The failing `gate.json` was deleted when the repair was queued, so I reproduced the gate verbatim to see the stderr.

## Fix (no authored Lean content touched)

Added the same worktree-root Lake shim the accepted sibling tasks use (`D9-*`, `D10-gaussian-toolbox`):

- `lean-toolchain` and `lake-manifest.json` (copies of the release package's pinned ones)
- `lakefile.toml` (mathlib require only; no Lean sources, no mathematical content)
- `.lake/packages` and `.lake/build/lib/lean` symlinks into `release/.lake`

The four authored files `release/Poincare/D10/TriangulationLowDim/{Complex,Models,Moise,Audit}.lean` are byte-identical to attempt 1 (SHA-256 verified).

